    <!-- Run it yourself (self-hosted) -->
    <section class="landing-section" id="self-hosted">
      <div class="landing-section-inner">
        <p class="section-label">Source-available. Install in your own harness.</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">Run it yourself</h2>

        <p>Prefer to run it yourself? Soleur is source-available and runs self-hosted on Claude Code, Grok Build, Codex, Devin CLI, and OpenCode today &mdash; the same {{ stats.agents }} agents and {{ stats.skills }} skills on each. Keep your knowledge base as plain files on your own machine, and join the waitlist if you want the hosted version when it opens.</p>

        <p>The blocks below install Soleur on each harness. The <a href="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code" rel="noopener noreferrer">Claude Code</a> path is the one with a published marketplace; the other four install from this repository and each has its own setup guide. Every harness needs its own session: nothing is shared between them.</p>

        <h3 class="section-subtitle">Claude Code</h3>

        <p>Self-hosted in Claude Code: signed in with your Claude plan or an Anthropic API key. This is the path with the published marketplace, and <strong>two commands</strong> is all it takes.</p>

        <!-- verified: 2026-08-12 source: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins -->
        <div class="quickstart-code">
          <pre><code>claude plugin marketplace add jikig-ai/soleur-marketplace
claude plugin install soleur@soleur-marketplace</code></pre>
        </div>

        <h3 class="section-subtitle">Grok Build</h3>

        <p>Soleur loads from this repository as a Grok Build plugin. Check it loaded first, then start a session:</p>

        <!-- verified: 2026-09-21 source: knowledge-base/engineering/grok-onboarding.md -->
        <div class="quickstart-code">
          <pre><code>grok inspect    # the soleur plugin, skills, agents, and MCP servers must appear
grok            # interactive session</code></pre>
        </div>

        <p>Full setup &mdash; subagent spawning, trust, and the command names Grok Build uses instead of Claude Code&rsquo;s &mdash; is in the <a href="{{ site.github }}/blob/main/knowledge-base/engineering/grok-onboarding.md" rel="noopener noreferrer">Grok Build onboarding guide</a>.</p>

        <h3 class="section-subtitle">Codex</h3>

        <p>Codex installs from a marketplace defined in this repository:</p>

        <!-- verified: 2026-09-11 source: knowledge-base/engineering/codex-onboarding.md -->
        <div class="quickstart-code">
          <pre><code>codex plugin marketplace add jikig-ai/soleur --sparse .agents/plugins --sparse plugins/soleur
codex plugin add soleur@soleur</code></pre>
        </div>

        <p>Then read the <a href="{{ site.github }}/blob/main/knowledge-base/engineering/codex-onboarding.md" rel="noopener noreferrer">Codex setup guide</a> for local development, updates, and compatibility details.</p>

        <h3 class="section-subtitle">Devin CLI</h3>

        <!-- verified: 2026-08-12 source: https://docs.devin.ai/cli -->
        <div class="quickstart-code">
          <pre><code>devin plugins install jikig-ai/soleur#plugins/soleur -y</code></pre>
        </div>

        <p>Use <code>-y</code> to skip the confirmation prompt. Devin <strong>Cloud</strong> sessions run under Soleur Cloud Mode &mdash; skills, rules, and MCP carry, but plugin subagents and session hooks do not. See the <a href="{{ site.github }}/blob/main/plugins/soleur/devin/INSTRUCTIONS.md" rel="noopener noreferrer">Devin compatibility instructions</a> for the cloud-vs-local capability matrix.</p>

        <h3 class="section-subtitle">OpenCode</h3>

        <p>Install Soleur into your OpenCode config directory via npm (this needs <code>bun</code> on <code>PATH</code>), then start a session. The installer vendors the payload into <code>~/.config/opencode/soleur/</code> (or run <code>bun plugins/soleur/scripts/install-opencode-adapter.ts</code> from a local checkout).</p>

        <!-- verified: 2026-10-22 source: plugins/soleur/opencode/INSTRUCTIONS.md -->
        <div class="quickstart-code">
          <pre><code>npx @soleur/opencode install
# or: bunx @soleur/opencode install
npx @soleur/opencode install --check    # prints opencode-install ok when the tree matches</code></pre>
        </div>

        <p>Commands are bare (<code>/go</code>, <code>/sync</code>, <code>/help</code>) and skills are invoked by bare id (<code>plan</code>, not <code>soleur:plan</code>), because OpenCode has no <code>soleur:</code> namespace. Two guards decide shell commands on OpenCode, and both run for real &mdash; a <code>deny</code> blocks the call, an <code>ask</code> opens a prompt &mdash; but they decide shell calls only: actions taken through OpenCode&rsquo;s code-mode <code>execute</code> are not covered. Soleur&rsquo;s operator-stage approval gate is not wired on OpenCode: those flows refuse rather than approve. OpenCode has no Stop hook, so the pipeline&rsquo;s <code>&lt;promise&gt;DONE&lt;/promise&gt;</code> completion marker is advisory: a finished gate sequence is reported rather than hard-stopped, and autonomous skills rely on their own structural checks. <code>/version</code> is installed but reports an unknown version, because the canonical command resolves the plugin through <code>CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT</code>, which this harness does not set. Full routing rules and the remaining capability differences: <a href="{{ site.github }}/blob/main/plugins/soleur/opencode/INSTRUCTIONS.md" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenCode instructions</a>.</p>

        <p>Claude Code: <code>/soleur:go</code>. Grok Build: <code>/go</code>. Codex: <code>$soleur:go</code>. Devin CLI: <code>/soleur:go</code>. OpenCode: <code>/go</code>.</p>
